# CPF North AutoStore Putaway Flow

Parent: [[CPF North AutoStore]]  
Related: [[TES Runtime Flows]], [[TES Workflow Concepts]], [[TES Axon Aggregates]]

## Configuration

Source: `resources/config/customers/ahs/cpf-north/workflows/cpf-north-autostore-workflow.csv`.

Active putaway configuration:

- Work request: `putaway-container`, type `container/putaway`.
- Workflow: `Autostore Putaway`.
- Steps: `preposition`, `putaway`, `return`; `hot-putaway` is an adhoc alternative.
- Resources: AutoStore preposition and return resources, plus decanting workstation `autostore-put-01`.
- Preposition end: `putaway-port`, typed `autostore-in-port`.
- Putaway starts at `putaway-port`; storage destination is an `autostore-tote` position in `autostore-zone`.
- Return starts at `return-port`.
- Active tasks: `put-container`, `handle-tote`, `preposition-tote`, and `return-tote`.
- Explicit task relations:
  - `handle-tote` created -> activate `preposition-tote`.
  - `handle-tote` completed -> activate `return-tote`.

## End-to-end event flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Source as Container/work request
    participant Engine as TES engine
    participant App as AsrsG2PApplication
    participant Station as Decanting station
    participant ASRS as AutoStore agent

    Source->>Engine: RequestWorkCreationCommand
    Engine->>Engine: Create work request and container
    Engine-->>App: READY put-container task request
    App->>Engine: RequestTaskAssignmentCommand
    Engine-->>Engine: TaskRequestAssignedEvent / ActivityTaskStartedEvent
    Engine->>Station: PICK_CONTAINER
    Station-->>Engine: CONTAINER_PICKED
    Engine->>Station: DROP_CONTAINER
    Station-->>Engine: CONTAINER_DROPPED
    Engine-->>Engine: put-container completed
    Engine->>Engine: handle-tote starts and currently completes immediately
    Engine->>ASRS: PREPOSITION_TOTE
    ASRS-->>Engine: tote movement completed
    Engine->>Station: item handling hook (currently incomplete)
    Engine->>ASRS: RETURN_TOTE
    ASRS-->>Engine: bin closed / tote returned
    Engine-->>Source: asset/work completion
```

## 1. Work request and task assignment

`WorkDispatcher` creates the work request and, on `WorkRequestReadyEvent`, requests tasks from accepted workflow relations.

The G2P application exposes ready putaway containers through:

`tes-agent/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/agent/application/g2p/asrs/AsrsG2PController.java`

Its `listContainers` query filters READY tasks with type `putaway/container/put-container`.

`AsrsG2PApplicationDef.assignContainers` then:

1. Resolves the selected workstation.
2. Finds READY put-container task requests.
3. Assigns each request to a staging position.
4. Creates or reuses a putaway task group of type `PutawayActivityType.CONTAINER`.
5. Sends `RequestTaskAssignmentCommand` with a `TaskRequestResource` and `MovePositionContext`.
6. Starts the group.

The task request assignment path is handled by:

`tes-engine/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/engine/core/workflow/activity/WorkflowActivityDef.java`

When the request is assigned, the activity creates the `put-container` activity task and starts it.

## 2. Container movement at the decanting workstation

The active task is `putaway/container/put-container`, implemented by:

`tes-activity/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/activity/putaway/task/PutawayContainerTaskDef.java`

Its resource event loop is:

1. `ActivityTaskStartedEvent` creates a `PICK_CONTAINER` equipment task at the source position.
2. `CONTAINER_PICKED` creates a `DROP_CONTAINER` equipment task from source to destination.
3. `CONTAINER_DROPPED` completes the activity.
4. `ActivityTaskCompletedEvent` with `PUT_CONTAINER` completes the asset activity at the end position.

The activity-level factory is:

`tes-activity/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/activity/putaway/PutawayActivityDef.java`

It selects the resource implementation by variant. A G2P port workstation uses `G2PPortWorkstationPutawayDef`; ordinary workstation/forklift variants use their corresponding move definitions.

## 3. Tote preposition and return

The active relation `handle-tote/preposition-tote` requests the storage move. The shared implementation is:

- `tes-activity/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/activity/preposition/task/PrepositionStorageMoveDef.java`
- `tes-activity/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/activity/preposition/PrepositionActivityDef.java`

The preposition path resolves the tote workflow asset and remaps a storage move to the staging/port position. For AutoStore it reaches:

- `tes-agent/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/agent/equipment/asrs/IAsrsController.java`: `PREPOSITION_TOTE` -> `prepositionBins`.
- `tes-agent/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/agent/equipment/asrs/AsrsController.java`: task-group and tote mapping.
- `tes-agent/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/agent/manufacturer/autostore/AutostoreController.java`: AutoStore API/log integration.

The return relation `handle-tote/return-tote` is activated on `task/completed`. Its active task is `return/storage/move`, and the AutoStore adapter maps `RETURN_TOTE` to `returnBin`. AutoStore closes the bin and emits the internal sequence represented by `BinClosed`, `PortClosed`, and tote-returned/resource completion events.

## 4. Item handling path and current implementation gap

The repository also contains an item-aware task:

`tes-activity/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/activity/putaway/task/PutawayContainerItemsTaskDef.java`

If selected, it would:

- pick the container;
- create one item put operation at a time;
- translate `ITEM_PUT` into `ActivityTaskExecution`;
- move the empty container to the end position;
- complete the activity.

However, the CPF North AutoStore CSV selects `handle-tote` (`putaway/container/handle-storage`) instead of `put-container-items`.

The selected handle task is implemented by:

`tes-activity/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/activity/putaway/task/PutawayHandleStorageDef.java`

Current behavior:

- On `ActivityTaskStartedEvent`, it immediately calls `completeTask`.
- On completion, it sends `CompleteWorkAssetCommand` for the workflow asset and then completes its superclass behavior.

The source comment says it should complete after items are put away, but the executable code does not wait for item events. In addition,:

`tes-activity/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/activity/putaway/resource/G2PPortWorkstationPutawayDef.java`

has the item-put invocation commented out and `putItems` empty. Therefore the configured event chain is structurally present, but the decant/item-handling business step is incomplete in this source snapshot.

## 5. State transitions to trace

For diagnostics, correlate:

- Work request: created -> ready -> task creation requested.
- Task request: created -> ready -> assignment requested -> assigned -> started -> completed.
- Activity task: created -> ready -> started -> executed/completion requested -> completed.
- Resource task: created -> submitted/dispatched -> started -> executed -> completed.
- Task group: created -> ready -> assigned -> started -> refreshed/paused/completed.
- AutoStore: port assigned/opened, movement started/completed, bin closed, port closed.

Definitions are in:

- `tes-coreapi/src/main/kotlin/com/onomatic/tes/coreapi/task/activity/events.kt`
- `tes-coreapi/src/main/kotlin/com/onomatic/tes/coreapi/task/resource/events.kt`
- `tes-coreapi/src/main/kotlin/com/onomatic/tes/coreapi/task/request/events.kt`
- `tes-coreapi/src/main/kotlin/com/onomatic/tes/coreapi/task/group/events.kt`
- `tes-coreapi/src/main/kotlin/com/onomatic/tes/coreapi/equipment/type/asrs/events.kt`
- `tes-coreapi/src/main/kotlin/com/onomatic/tes/coreapi/equipment/type/forklift/definitions.kt`

## Traceability

- G2P application: `tes-activity/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/activity/g2p/application/AsrsG2PApplicationDef.java`
- Agent controller: `tes-agent/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/agent/application/g2p/asrs/AsrsG2PController.java`
- Activity orchestration: `tes-engine/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/engine/core/workflow/activity/WorkflowActivityDef.java`
- Dispatch and work creation: `tes-engine/src/main/java/com/onomatic/tes/engine/core/dispatcher/WorkDispatcher.java`
